* `NavigatorDispatchArithmetic`          — Reflection 350 (a position-indexed navigator splits DECISION from CORRECTNESS: the bottom-up locator's branch dispatch is pure offset/length arithmetic, balance is demoted to the correctness side — the PROBE that settled `(i'-b-B2c-nested-fbc-emission-locator)`, `move_trichotomy`/`move_exclusive` pure `omega`, `#guard`ed on three witnesses in `Tests/Guards/Proofs/SeqNestedEntryLocateProbe.lean`. R349 left the emission-spine-walk LOCATOR as the residual; the probe asks its single-step shape — (a) one offset-tracked `body.length` recursion, or (b) a separate balance-locate front end. FINDING (option a): a navigator over a recursive deliverable splits into a DECISION procedure (which branch) and a CORRECTNESS justification (why); the decision is the cheap part. Walking `RecSeqBody body` with base offset `off`, the head entry `e` occupies `[off, off+e.length-1]`, so the target window start `a` selects the move by comparing `a` against `off+1` and `off+e.length` ALONE — leaf (`a=off+1`) / descend (`off+1<a<off+e.length`, off'=off+1) / advance (`off+e.length<a`, off'=off+e.length+1), `a=off+e.length` the impossible separator/close (`navMove`/`classifyMove` total, `classify_leaf`/`_descend`/`_advance`/`move_exhaustive`/`move_exclusive` pure `omega`). The structure STORES each entry's length and the offset-slice invariant `body=(take H).drop off` ties it to absolute coordinates, so the navigator NEVER calls balance to decide. BALANCE IS DEMOTED to correctness: R330's TOP-DOWN projection selected the entry by `flowBracketBalance=0` (it had a token coordinate, had to FIND the entry); this BOTTOM-UP locator keyed on `[a,b)` locates by offset arithmetic, balance entering only the PROOF that the slice equals the window (via all-seq-path/`WellTyped`), never the selector (`topDown_needs_balance` vs `bottomUp_decides_by_arithmetic`). THE RULE: before importing a locate's heavy front end into a navigator descending the same structure, ask w