* `MetricBridgeIsComposition`               — Reflection 310 (a feared "bridge between two PARALLEL metrics" is often ALREADY a theorem: a STRUCTURAL count and a NUMERIC count that share a substrate are equated by COMPOSITION, not a new per-step induction — the toy of `flowBracketBalance_pos_of_btFold_head`, the gate→hypothesis bridge of `(i'-b-locator-glue-gate-bridge)`. A token stream (`op b` pushes a `Bool`, `cl` pops, `neu` neutral) carries two metrics: the NUMERIC `bal` (fold of `{+1, -1, 0}`) and the STRUCTURAL `fold` (a `List Bool`, its LENGTH the metric). The de-risk feared they might DIVERGE (push map vs seq differently), needing a per-step induction relating pushes to deltas. **Correction 1 (POSITIVE `bridge`)**: they do not — both reduce to the SAME substrate `bal` via `foldLen` (`stack length = bal`), so `bridge` (non-empty stack ⇒ `bal ≥ 1`) is `foldLen` + "non-empty ⇒ length ≥ 1" + `omega`; the per-step reconciliation the de-risk feared IS `foldLen`, which already exists. **Type-agnostic dividend (POSITIVE)**: `bridge` takes `= some hd` for an ARBITRARY `hd : Bool` — the proof is blind to the head value, so ONE lemma serves both axes (`bridgeTrue`/`bridgeFalse`, seq/map). **Correction 2 (NEGATIVE, `#guard`-backed)**: the fear is legitimate IN GENERAL — a WRONG metric `wfold` (pushes only on `op true`, ignoring `op false`) genuinely diverges: on `diverge = [op false, op true]`, `#guard (fold …).map (·.length) == some 2` and `bal == 2` (real metrics coincide) but `#guard (wfold …).map (·.length) == some 1` (≠ `bal`). So VERIFY the substrate is shared (every `op _` pushes uniformly AND contributes `+1`); don't assume divergence (author an induction) NOR coincidence (skip the check). Sharpens [[ref-probe-deferred-universal-before-producing]] on the metric-unification axis, as [[ref-backward-locator-mirrors-forward]] did on the machinery axis)
