* `WidenedSlotPinnedBySibling`              — Reflection 619 (widening ONE conjunct of a conjunctive invariant buys nothing while a SIBLING conjunct still constrains the same variables — and the sibling that pins it is usually the one no consumer in that region reads. The accumulation invariant carried `PendingNode false sp_start sp_flow sp_scan` beside `sc.flowLevel ≥ 1 → GStar SSWhite sp_flow sp_scan`, the second added for ONE purpose: a flow-interior plain scalar ends its production before the whitespace `collectPlainScalarLoop` then consumes, so inside a flow collection the accumulator legitimately sits a run behind the cursor. That room was never occupied. Inside an open flow collection the only DERIVABLE `PendingNode` constructor is `noPending : PendingNode false sp_start sp sp` — every other one demands a stream- or document-level witness AT `sp_flow`, and an unclosed flow collection has none — so the widened slot was provably always `GStar.nil`, every producer discharged it that way, and the arm that needed it (`accum_step_content`'s plain-scalar case at depth ≥ 1) could not be written at all. §1 `pend_pins_the_endpoints` is `cases` on a two-constructor inductive and is axiom-FREE, which is the point: the pin was never hard to see, it was never LOOKED at. §2 `widened_slot_is_dead` derives the equality from the invariant itself and `no_room_for_the_step` shows the failure's actual shape — not a hard goal but an EMPTY hypothesis. §3–§4 the repair: the pinning conjunct was not wrong, it was OVER-SCOPED. `same_at_depth_zero` is the whole soundness argument for re-scoping it to `flowLevel = 0` (one line, an iff at the only depth anything reads it) and `strictly_weaker_at_depth` confirms the change is real, not a rename — the mirror of Reflection 617's `inv'_is_strictly_stronger`, where an invariant had to GROW to imply a new guard; here it SHRINKS to stop implying an old equation. §5–§6 the cheap diagnostic that would have found it: `rescoping_is_sound` over a th