* `CoverageIsBranchTimesFrame`              — Reflection 667 (a call site's coverage is its BRANCH times its FRAME. Once a producer is merged over a case split ([[PuntTheShapeNotTheSite]]) and each branch needs a different optional argument, a site is served on a branch only if the caller's evidence lemma can REACH that branch and the caller's pending can OFFER the frame it needs — so `covers = sees && offers ∘ needs`, and the product is computable from types alone before any call is written, because which branches a caller sees is a property of the lemma it destructured (a break-free analysis returns one) and which frames it offers is a property of its slot (`SBlockIndented` has a compact alternative, `SBlockNode` does not). Reading either factor alone gets a cell wrong (`neither_factor_alone_predicts`), and an empty product is silent: the call typechecks and returns `True` forever. **An empty cell is NOT a boundary** — the two questions of [[PuntMayBeTheBoundary]] and the split of [[PuntTheShapeNotTheSite]] both need a datum that is FALSE somewhere, and nothing here is false: each factor of the empty product is shared with a site that IS served (`the_branch_factor_is_not_fatal`, `the_frame_factor_is_not_fatal`), so the emptiness belongs to the PAIR (`emptiness_is_a_property_of_the_pair`) and relaxing either factor closes it (`either_relaxation_closes_it`), which a boundary never permits. Corollary in the same table: the route's side condition — items 39's boundary and 40's decidable split — is VACUOUS here, because the only sites that reach the branch testing it carry index 0 (`the_side_condition_is_vacuous_where_it_can_fire`), so one inequality is a boundary, a shape or nothing depending only on which sites reach it. L4YAML item 41, 2026-08-17: `entryPropsKeyPack_of_dispatch` gives item 17's `PropsKeyPack` the route item 38 gave the scalar pack, merged over the landing disjunct as in item 40, so `- &p a: 1`, `-⏎  &p a: 1`, `k:⏎  &p a: 1` and `  - &p a: 1` compose